Ritemark Configuration Defaults (Sprint 107 R1, GH #—): product.json
`configurationDefaults` apply on DESKTOP.

VS Code only reads configuration defaults from product.json on the WEB
workbench (environmentService.options). Ritemark's branding block
(trust off, *.md → ritemark.editor, theme, tree/indent, preview off)
was therefore dead on desktop — the "md opens as code + trust dialog"
first-run bug. This patch:
  - adds `configurationDefaults` to IProductConfiguration
  - registers `product.configurationDefaults` in DefaultConfiguration
    (additive; user/workspace settings still override)

diff --git a/src/vs/base/common/product.ts b/src/vs/base/common/product.ts
index a352bdd7d61..82a29046dc1 100644
--- a/src/vs/base/common/product.ts
+++ b/src/vs/base/common/product.ts
@@ -65,6 +65,14 @@ export type ExtensionVirtualWorkspaceSupport = {
 };
 
 export interface IProductConfiguration {
+	/**
+	 * Ritemark (Sprint 107 R1): default configuration overrides contributed by
+	 * the product, applied like extension-contributed configurationDefaults but
+	 * sourced from product.json. Desktop path — the web workbench reads the
+	 * equivalent from IWorkbenchConstructionOptions.configurationDefaults.
+	 */
+	readonly configurationDefaults?: Record<string, unknown>;
+
 	readonly version: string;
 	readonly date?: string;
 	readonly quality?: string;
